New at SovereignLab: a community board for our weekly game.

Players kept asking how others approach the weekly Case Files and Town Hall challenges. Now there is a place to compare notes: tips, strategy, highlights and run results, without sharing who you are.

How it works:

• Subscribers get an email invite and join under a random handle like Bright-Falcon-4821. No email, name or photo is stored with it.

• Before a post is saved, a scanner hides emails, phone numbers, addresses, links and ID numbers. Posts are also encrypted where they are stored.
• A new player’s first three posts are checked by a person, and two reports hide a post.

• Private groups (18+) are end-to-end encrypted in your browser, so only members can read them, not even us. Messages delete after 30 days.
• Kid-mode players never see the board.

Honest limits: no scanner catches everything, and anyone can screenshot what they see, so we ask everyone to keep personal details out entirely.
